<div class=3D"sect2">
<h3 id=3D"_conclusion"><a class=3D"anchor" href=3D"https://docs.vulkan.org/=
tutorial/latest/Building_a_Simple_Engine/Engine_Architecture/03_component_s=
ystems.html#_conclusion"></a>Conclusion</h3>
<div class=3D"paragraph">
<p>Component systems provide a flexible and modular approach to building ga=
me objects in your engine. By following the principles outlined in this sec=
tion, you can create a robust component system that:</p>
</div>
<div class=3D"olist arabic">
<ol class=3D"arabic">
<li>
<p>Promotes code reuse through composition</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Reduces coupling between different parts of your engine</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Allows for flexible entity creation without deep inheritance hierarchies=
</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Can be optimized for performance</p>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class=3D"paragraph">
<p>In the next section, we=E2=80=99ll explore resource management systems, =
which are crucial for efficiently handling assets in your engine.</p>
</div>
<div class=3D"paragraph">
<p><a href=3D"https://docs.vulkan.org/tutorial/latest/Building_a_Simple_Eng=
ine/Engine_Architecture/02_architectural_patterns.html" class=3D"xref page"=
>Previous: Architectural Patterns</a> | <a href=3D"https://docs.vulkan.org/=
tutorial/latest/Building_a_Simple_Engine/Engine_Architecture/04_resource_ma=
nagement.html" class=3D"xref page">Next: Resource Management</a></p>
</div>
</div>
